Package: shapCopula
Type: Package
Title: Inference for Conditional Shapley Values via Copulas
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Agostino", "Gnasso",
    email = "agostino.gnasso@unina.it",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8046-3923"))
Author: Agostino Gnasso [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Agostino Gnasso <agostino.gnasso@unina.it>
Description: Implements the one-step cross-fitted estimator for Conditional
    SAGE (Shapley Additive Global importancE) values introduced in Gnasso
    (2026). The conditional value function E[f(X) | X_S = x_S] is estimated
    via a Gaussian copula with empirical marginals (default) or a
    nonparametric vine copula ('rvinecopulib'). The estimator uses K-fold
    cross-fitting and a U-statistic debiasing step to yield asymptotically
    valid Wald confidence intervals and two-sided hypothesis tests for global
    feature importance. A marginal (interventional) SAGE baseline is included
    for comparison with standard SHAP-based attributions.
